"tutorial18_1" = "To multiply easily on the abacus, you need to know the times tables by heart.";
"tutorial18_3" = "While doing a test, you can tap the “Rule Book” at the top right to see the times tables.";
"tutorial18_4" = "Now let's start the lesson.";
"tutorial18_5" = "Multiplication on the abacus is done place by place and added up, just like regular multiplication.";
"tutorial18_6" = "What we'll do is multiply 6 by each place, starting from the smallest, and add them up.";
"tutorial18_7" = "We multiply 6 by 4 and write the result in the ones place.";
"tutorial18_8" = "Then we'll multiply 6 by 2.";
"tutorial18_9" = "6 is in the ones place, and 2 is in the tens place.";
"tutorial18_10" = "When we multiply the ones by the tens, we add the result to the tens place on the abacus.";
"tutorial18_11" = "We multiply 3 by 2 and write it in the ones place.";
"tutorial18_12" = "Then we'll multiply 1 by 3.";
"tutorial18_13" = "1 is in the tens place and 3 is in the ones place.";
"tutorial18_14" = "When we multiply the tens by the ones, the result is added to the tens place.";
"tutorial18_15" = "The answer is 36.";
"tutorial18_16" = "Finally, let's look at this example.";
"tutorial18_17" = "We multiply 8 by 3 and write the result in the ones place.";
"tutorial18_18" = "Now we multiply 5 by 3 and write it in the tens place.";
"tutorial18_19" = "The answer is 174.";
"tutorial18_20" = "Multiply 3 by 6 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_105" = "Enter 18 on the abacus.";
"tutorial18_21" = "Now we'll multiply 3 by the 4 in the tens place and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial18_22" = "When we multiply the ones by the tens, where does the answer go on the abacus?";
"tutorial_ipucu_106" = "Think of it like multiplying 10 by 1. 10 x 1 = 10. So it goes in the tens place.";
"tutorial_sik_034" = "In the ones place.";
"tutorial_sik_035" = "In the tens place";
"tutorial_sik_036" = "In the hundreds place.";
"tutorial18_23" = "Multiply the 4 in the tens place by 3 and add the result to the tens place on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_107" = "Add 12 to the tens place. That means adding 120 on the abacus.";
"tutorial18_24" = "The answer is 138.";
"tutorial19_1" = "When multiplying, we may need to use the addition rules.";
"tutorial19_2" = "First I multiply 6 by 7 and write the result in the ones place.";
"tutorial19_3" = "Then I'll multiply 6 by 9 and write the result in the tens place.";
"tutorial19_4" = "When writing 54 in the tens place, I can add the 50 directly.";
"tutorial19_5" = "But I can't add the 4 directly.";
"tutorial19_6" = "So I'll use a rule.";
"tutorial19_7" = "I add it with small friends.";
"tutorial19_8" = "The answer is 582.";
"tutorial19_9" = "I multiply 6 by 4 and write the result in the ones place.";
"tutorial19_10" = "Then I'll multiply 6 by 8 and write the result in the tens place.";
"tutorial19_11" = "When writing 48 in the tens place, I can add the 40 directly.";
"tutorial19_12" = "But I can't add the 8 directly.";
"tutorial19_13" = "I'll add it with big friends.";
"tutorial19_14" = "Add 10. Take away its friend, 2.";
"tutorial19_15" = "The answer is 504.";
"tutorial19_22" = "If you've forgotten how addition works, go back and look at the addition part.";
"tutorial19_16" = "Multiply 9 by 8 and write it in the ones place.";
"tutorial_ipucu_108" = "Enter 72 on the abacus.";
"tutorial19_17" = "Now we'll multiply 9 by 4 and add it to the tens place.";
"tutorial19_18" = "9 x 4 = 36. First add the 30.";
"tutorial_ipucu_109" = "Add 30 to the tens place. That means adding 300 on the abacus.";
"tutorial19_19" = "Now decide which rule to use to add the 6.";
"tutorial19_23" = "Which addition rule will you use?";
"tutorial_ipucu_110" = "In the big friends step 'Add 10. Take away 6's friend, 4', we can't take away the 4, so we'll add it with Mixed Friends.";
"tutorial9_1002" = "Add 6 to the tens place using mixed friends.";
"tutorial_ipucu_111" = "In the tens place, do these steps: add 1, take away 5, add 10. That means: add 10 on the abacus, take away 50, add 100.";
"tutorial_kural_048" = "Add 1. Take away 5. Add 10.";
"tutorial19_21" = "And the answer is 432.";
"tutorial20_1" = "In this lesson, we'll multiply 2-digit numbers by 2-digit numbers.";
"tutorial20_2" = "The part to watch out for:";
"tutorial20_3" = "When we multiply ones by ones, the result goes in the ones place on the abacus.";
"tutorial20_4" = "5 times 3 equals 15.";
"tutorial20_5" = "We write it so the ones digit of the result lands on the ones place of the abacus.";
"tutorial20_6" = "When we multiply ones by tens, the result goes in the tens place.";
"tutorial20_8" = "We multiply 4 by 3 and write it so the ones digit of the result lands on the tens place of the abacus.";
"tutorial20_9" = "When we multiply tens by tens, the result goes in the hundreds place.";
"tutorial20_10" = "3 times 6 equals 18.";
"tutorial20_11" = "We write it so the ones digit of the result lands on the hundreds place.";
"tutorial20_12" = "We start multiplying from the ones place of the 2nd number.";
"tutorial20_13" = "First we multiply 1 by 3 and add it to the ones place.";
"tutorial20_14" = "Now we multiply 1 by 4 and add it to the tens place.";
"tutorial20_15" = "We add the tens digit of the 2nd number the same way.";
"tutorial20_16" = "We multiply 2 by 3 and add it to the tens place.";
"tutorial20_17" = "We multiply 2 by 4 and add it to the hundreds place.";
"tutorial20_18" = "The answer is 903.";
"tutorial20_20" = "First we multiply 3 by 8 and add it to the ones place.";
"tutorial20_21" = "Now we multiply 3 by 7 and add it to the tens place.";
"tutorial20_22" = "We multiply 4 by 8 and add it to the tens place.";
"tutorial20_23" = "We multiply 4 by 7 and add it to the hundreds place.";
"tutorial20_100" = "The answer is 3354.";
"tutorial20_24" = "We'll start from the ones place of the 2nd number.";
"tutorial20_30" = "Multiply 4 by 9 and decide which place on the abacus to add the result to.";
"tutorial20_31" = "Which place will you add it to?";
"tutorial_ipucu_112" = "Think of it like multiplying 1 by 1. 1 x 1 = 1. So it goes in the ones place.";
"tutorial20_25" = "Multiply 4 by 9 and add the result to the ones place on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_113" = "4 x 9 = 36. Enter 36 on the abacus.";
"tutorial20_32" = "Multiply 4 by 6 and decide which place on the abacus to add the result to.";
"tutorial_ipucu_114" = "Think of it like multiplying 10 by 1. 10 x 1 = 10. So it goes in the tens place.";
"tutorial20_33" = "Multiply 4 by 6 and add the result to the tens place on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_115" = "4 x 6 = 24. Add 24 to the tens place. That means adding 240 on the abacus.";
"tutorial20_34" = "Multiply 5 by 9 and decide which place on the abacus to add the result to.";
"tutorial20_35" = "Multiply 5 by 9 and add the result to the tens place on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_116" = "5 x 9 = 45. Add 45 to the tens place. That means adding 450 on the abacus.";
"tutorial20_36" = "Multiply 5 by 6 and decide which place on the abacus to add the result to.";
"tutorial_ipucu_117" = "Think of it like multiplying 10 by 10. 10 x 10 = 100. So it goes in the hundreds place.";
"tutorial20_37" = "Multiply 5 by 6 and add the result to the hundreds place on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_118" = "5 x 6 = 30. Add 30 to the hundreds place. That means adding 3000 on the abacus.";
"tutorial20_29" = "The answer is 3726.";
"tutorial21_1" = "In this lesson, we'll multiply 3-digit numbers by 1-digit numbers.";
"tutorial21_2" = "In addition to what we learned before,";
"tutorial21_3" = "when we multiply hundreds by ones, the result goes in the hundreds place.";
"tutorial21_5" = "We write it so the ones digit of the result lands on the hundreds place of the abacus.";
"tutorial21_6" = "If you don't know which place to write it in, you can figure it out by putting 1s and 0s in place of the digits.";
"tutorial21_7" = "For example, 100 x 1 = 100. So when hundreds are multiplied by ones, the result goes in the hundreds place.";
"tutorial21_8" = "10 x 10 = 100. When tens are multiplied by tens, the result goes in the hundreds.";
"tutorial21_9" = "Let's solve an example.";
"tutorial21_10" = "I multiply one place at a time, starting from the smallest.";
"tutorial21_11" = "4x4 = 16. I write it in the ones place.";
"tutorial21_12" = "4x8 = 32. I write it in the tens place.";
"tutorial21_13" = "2x4 = 8. I add it to the hundreds place.";
"tutorial21_14" = "The answer is 1136.";
"tutorial21_15" = "Multiply 6 by 3 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_119" = "6x3=18. Enter 18 on the abacus.";
"tutorial21_16" = "Multiply 6 by the 2 in the tens place and add the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_120" = "6x2=12. Since we're multiplying tens by ones, add 12 to the tens place on the abacus. That means adding 120 on the abacus.";
"tutorial21_17" = "Multiply 6 by the 7 in the hundreds place and add the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_121" = "6x7=42. Since we're multiplying hundreds by ones, add 42 to the hundreds place on the abacus. That means adding 4200 on the abacus.";
"tutorial21_18" = "The answer is 4338.";
"tutorial22_1" = "In this lesson, we'll multiply 3-digit numbers by 2-digit numbers.";
"tutorial22_2" = "In addition to what we learned before:";
"tutorial22_3" = "When we multiply hundreds by tens, the result goes in the thousands place.";
"tutorial22_4" = "The result of 6x2 is 12.";
"tutorial22_5" = "We write it so the ones digit of the result lands on the thousands place of the abacus.";
"tutorial22_25" = "The answer is 12000.";
"tutorial22_6" = "Let's solve this example.";
"tutorial22_7" = "I'll multiply one place at a time, starting from the smallest place of the 2nd number.";
"tutorial22_8" = "3x1 = 3. I write it in the ones place.";
"tutorial22_100" = "3x2 = 6. I write it in the tens place.";
"tutorial22_10" = "3x3 = 9. I write it in the hundreds place.";
"tutorial22_11" = "I move on to the next place.";
"tutorial22_12" = "2x1 = 2. I write it in the tens place.";
"tutorial22_13" = "2x2 = 4. I write it in the hundreds place.";
"tutorial22_14" = "2x3 = 6. I write it in the thousands place.";
"tutorial22_15" = "And the answer is 7383.";
"tutorial22_16" = "We'll multiply starting from the smallest place of the 2nd number and add the results to the abacus one at a time.";
"tutorial22_17" = "Multiply 2 by 2 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_122" = "2x2=4. Ones times ones. Write 4 in the ones place on the abacus.";
"tutorial22_18" = "Multiply 2 by 1 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_123" = "2x1=2. Ones times tens. Write 2 in the tens place on the abacus. That means adding 20 on the abacus.";
"tutorial22_19" = "Multiply 2 by 3 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_124" = "2x3=6. Ones times hundreds. Write 6 in the hundreds place on the abacus. That means adding 600 on the abacus.";
"tutorial22_20" = "We move on to the next place.";
"tutorial22_21" = "Multiply 4 by 2 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_125" = "4x2=8. Ones times tens. Write 8 in the tens place on the abacus. That means adding 80 on the abacus.";
"tutorial22_22" = "Multiply 4 by 1 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_126" = "4x1=4. Tens times tens. Write 4 in the hundreds place on the abacus. That means adding 400 on the abacus.";
"tutorial22_23" = "Multiply 4 by 3 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_127" = "4x3=12. Hundreds times tens. Write 12 in the thousands place on the abacus. That means adding 12000 on the abacus.";
"tutorial22_24" = "The answer is 13104.";
"tutorial22_26" = "Which of the options below is wrong?";
"tutorial_ipucu_128" = "Think of it like multiplying 10 by 1. 10 x 1 = 10. So when tens are multiplied by ones, the answer goes in the tens place.";
"tutorial_sik_037" = "When tens are multiplied by tens, the result goes in the hundreds.";
"tutorial_sik_038" = "When hundreds are multiplied by tens, the result goes in the thousands.";
"tutorial_sik_039" = "When tens are multiplied by ones, the result goes in the ones.";
"tutorial23_1" = "7x6 = 42. I write it in the ones place.";
"tutorial23_2" = "7x8 = 56. I write it in the tens place.";
"tutorial23_3" = "7x5 = 35. I write it in the hundreds place.";
"tutorial23_4" = "9x6 = 54. I write it in the tens place.";
"tutorial23_5" = "9x8 = 72. I write it in the hundreds place.";
"tutorial23_6" = "9x5 = 45. I write it in the thousands place.";
"tutorial23_7" = "And the answer is 56842.";
"tutorial23_8" = "We'll multiply starting from the smallest place of the 2nd number and add to the abacus one at a time.";
"tutorial23_9" = "Multiply 4 by 5 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_129" = "4x5=20. Ones times ones. Write 20 in the ones place on the abacus. That means adding 20 on the abacus.";
"tutorial23_10" = "Multiply 4 by 6 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_130" = "4x6=24. Ones times tens. Write 24 in the tens place on the abacus. That means adding 240 on the abacus.";
"tutorial23_12" = "Multiply 4 by 7 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_131" = "4x7=28. Ones times hundreds. Write 28 in the hundreds place on the abacus. That means adding 2800 on the abacus.";
"tutorial23_13" = "Multiply 8 by 5 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_132" = "8x5=40. Ones times tens. Write 40 in the tens place on the abacus. That means adding 400 on the abacus.";
"tutorial23_14" = "Multiply 8 by 6 and enter the result on the abacus.";
"tutorial_ipucu_133" = "8x6=48. Tens times tens. Write 48 in the hundreds place on the abacus. That means adding 4800 on the abacus.";
"tutorial23_15" = "Multiply 8 by 7 and enter the result on the abacus.";
